+## Symbolic links
+
+Zip archives and squashfs images can contain symbolic links. These are
+skipped by default, with a notice in the log saying how many were
+skipped.
+
+With `-l` / `--links` each symbolic link is listed as a regular file
+with a `.rclonelink` suffix whose contents are the link target. This
+lets `rclone copy --links` recreate the link on a destination which
+supports symlinks, such as the local backend.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular file in the archive whose name happens to end in
+`.rclonelink` is still treated as a regular file.
+
